sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Authenticated Envelope Creation Acceptance and Replay Rejection
  accDescr: A coordinator signs in and requests an envelope for a consultation. Laravel authorizes the role and assignment, minimizes the record, and asks OpenSSL AES 256 GCM to encrypt it using a key from the ignored keyring. The adviser signs in and submits the envelope. Laravel authenticates the envelope and adviser, stores one unique replay receipt, and returns plaintext. A second submission is rejected with conflict and is audited without plaintext.
  actor coordinator as Coordinator
  participant flutter as Flutter Web
  participant api as Laravel API
  participant crypto as OpenSSL AES 256 GCM
  participant keyring as Protected keyring
  participant db as MariaDB
  actor adviser as Assigned adviser
  coordinator->>flutter: Choose consultation and prepare secure envelope
  flutter->>api: HTTPS POST with bearer session and consultation ID
  api->>db: Authorize coordinator and read minimized assigned record
  api->>keyring: Read active key by key ID
  api->>crypto: Encrypt plaintext with random nonce and authenticated metadata
  crypto-->>api: Ciphertext and authentication tag
  api-->>flutter: 201 short lived envelope without key
  adviser->>flutter: Paste coordinator provided envelope
  flutter->>api: HTTPS POST envelope with adviser session
  api->>keyring: Load key identified by authenticated metadata
  api->>crypto: Verify tag and decrypt
  crypto-->>api: Authenticated plaintext or safe failure
  api->>db: Authorize assigned adviser and insert unique message receipt
  api-->>flutter: 200 minimized record with no store header
  flutter->>api: Repeat the same accepted envelope
  api->>db: Unique message ID conflicts
  api-->>flutter: 409 replay rejected with correlation reference
